SonosDial 1.2.0 — license scope

The Windows assistant (installer/app.py, installer/device.py and installer/i18n.py),
including its integrated use of esptool, is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later.
Full license: licenses/GPL-3.0.txt. Corresponding source and build scripts are
included, and the complete companion source archive is installed with the app.

The project's own ESP32 firmware application, documentation and remaining own
helper scripts and original logo assets are MIT-licensed: licenses/MIT-SonosDial.txt.

Third-party components retain their original licenses and copyright notices.
Arduino-ESP32: LGPL-2.1-or-later, with source, replaceable objects/archives and
a tested relink recipe under firmware-relink in the full release source asset.
TinyXML2: zlib. ArduinoJson: MIT.
See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md for the complete mapping.

The earlier MIT notice for the assistant's own source is preserved for historical
attribution. The desktop application distributed together with esptool is
explicitly GPL-3.0-or-later. The firmware is a separate program and is not
automatically relicensed as GPL by being included in the same download.

Legal license texts under licenses are original, untranslated copies.
